  "worked_solution": "The given equation is equivalent to \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}\u2061(\\frac{x}{2}-\\frac{\\pi }{8})=-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}.\n$$\n\nSo, the general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x}{2}-\\frac{\\pi }{8} & =-\\frac{\\pi }{6}+n\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the above equation for $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x}{2} & =\\frac{\\pi }{8}-\\frac{\\pi }{6}+n\\pi  \\\\ \\frac{x}{2} & =-\\frac{\\pi }{24}+n\\pi  \\\\ x & =-\\frac{\\pi }{12}+2n\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have that $a=-\\frac{1}{12}.$",
